>> title: Bulgogi Marinade
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: korean, beef, soy sauce, marinade, grill
>> counters: Ramen Shop
>> aka: bulgogi, bulgogi sauce, pulgogi, Korean BBQ beef marinade
>> pairs-with: haemul-pajeon
>> servings: 4
>> time: 15 min
>> slack: forgiving — the pear's enzyme keeps working: meat left in this for a day and a half goes soft and mealy rather than tender
>> step.1: grate into a bowl
>> step.2: whisk in
>> step.3: stir in
>> step.4: fold in, marinate 2 hr

Grate @Asian pear{1/2}(peeled and cored), @yellow onion{1/4}(small), and @garlic{5%cloves} into a #bowl{}.

Whisk @soy sauce{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @dark brown sugar{3%Tbs}(38 g), and @mirin{2%Tbs}(30 mL) into @&(~1)grated pear{} until the sugar dissolves.

Stir @toasted sesame oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @toasted sesame seeds{1%Tbs}, and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)marinade{}.

Fold @scallions{2}(thinly sliced) into @&(~1)marinade{}, then marinate 2 lb of thinly sliced ribeye in it for ~{2%hr}.
